<headroom-library version="1" id="crunch-terrace-anthem-stack" category="Crunch" order="180" instrument="guitar" style="Britpop">
  <description>Humbuckers into a loud master-volume British stack with a low-gain overdrive in front: a thick, compressed, sustaining wall for big anthemic strummed chords and simple, singable leads, with a plate glow behind it. Strum hard, let chords ring, layer it.</description>
  <tags><tag>Crunch</tag><tag>Britpop</tag><tag>Rhythm</tag><tag>Humbucker</tag><tag>Overdrive</tag><tag>Plate Reverb</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.groundguitar.com/tone-breakdown/noel-gallaghers-gear-on-definitely-maybe/" title="Ground Guitar: Noel Gallagher's gear on Definitely Maybe"/>
    <source url="https://www.groundguitar.com/noel-gallagher-gear/" title="Ground Guitar: Noel Gallagher's guitars, amps and gear list"/>
    <source url="https://www.sweetwater.com/insync/the-history-of-the-legendary-marshall-jcm800-2203/" title="Sweetwater InSync: the history of the Marshall JCM800 2203"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
